arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App shipment tracker for a logistics company. The project has already been scaffolded at:
- Server project: /tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/
- Client project: /tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/

It was created with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. This means:
- Global Interactive Auto mode (all pages interactive by default)
- Two projects: server hosts, .Client has all interactive UI components
- Interactive components MUST go in the .Client project
- Data access from .Client must go through HTTP APIs (no direct DbContext access from .Client)
- ASP.NET Core Identity is configured with SQLite

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Models (in .Client project since both sides need them)

Create `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 2. Service Interface (in .Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 3. Client-side implementation (HttpClient-based, in .Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
    }
}
```

### 4. Server-side implementation (direct data access, in server project)

Create `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ShipmentServerService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;

    public ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db)
    {
        _db = db;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments
            .Where(s => s.CustomerEmail == customerEmail)
            .OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate)
            .ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await _db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
            await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }
    }
}
```

### 5. Update ApplicationDbContext to include Shipments DbSet

Edit `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```
And add to the class:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

### 6. API Endpoints

Create `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Endpoints/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;

using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentEndpoints(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("", async (ApplicationDbContext db) =>
            await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync());

        group.MapGet("track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
        {
            var shipment = await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
            return shipment is not null ? Results.Ok(shipment) : Results.NotFound();
        });

        group.MapGet("customer/{customerEmail}", async (string customerEmail, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
            await db.Shipments
                .Where(s => s.CustomerEmail == Uri.UnescapeDataString(customerEmail))
                .OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate)
                .ToListAsync());

        group.MapPut("{id}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
        {
            var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
            if (shipment is null) return Results.NotFound();
            shipment.Status = status;
            await db.SaveChangesAsync();
            return Results.Ok();
        });
    }
}
```

### 7. Update Server Program.cs

In `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`:
- Add `using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Services;` and `using ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;`
- After `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEmailSender<ApplicationUser>, IdentityNoOpEmailSender>();` add:
  `builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();`
- Before `app.Run();` add:
  `app.MapShipmentEndpoints();`

### 8. Update Client Program.cs

Edit `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>(client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 9. Pages (in .Client project)

**Delete** the following template files:
- `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Counter.razor`
- `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Weather.razor`

**Replace Home.razor** at `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`:
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Tracker</h1>
<p class="lead">Welcome to the logistics shipment tracking system.</p>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <p>You are logged in as <strong>@context.User.Identity?.Name</strong>.</p>
        <p>Use the navigation menu to access shipment tracking features.</p>
    </Authorized>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <p>Please <a href="Account/Login">log in</a> to track shipments or manage dispatches.</p>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
```

**Create Dispatcher page** at `/tmp/sv-a8131b0adae74c2eb7a1d54a1dc6de5b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Dispatch.razor`:
```razor
@page "/dispatch"
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize]
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>Dispatch - Shipments</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Dispatch</h1>

<div class="mb-3">
    <input type="text" class="form-control" placeholder="Filter by destination..."
           @bind="filterText" @bind:event="oninput" />
</div>

@if (shipments is null)
{
    <p><em>Loading shipments...</em></p>
}
else if (!FilteredShipments.Any())
{
    <p>No shipments found.</p>
}
